1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-10425
2 CONT 1.  John, King of England, conspired unsuccessfully with Philip II ofFran ce to supplant his older brother, Richard, as King of England whenRicha rd left on the Third Crusade.  On Richard's death, Joh
2 CONC n ascended tothe th rone to the exclusion of his nephew Arthur I of Brittany, who,aided by Ph ilip II of France, began a revolt in France.  John's reignwas 1199 - 121 6.  Burkes Peerage records 1160 a
2 CONC s date of birth.
2 CONT Although Arthur was captured (1202), John lost many of his Frenchpossessi ons to Philip.
2 CONT John objected to Pope Innocent III's choice for archbishop of Canterburya nd the pope placed England under an interdict March 24, 1208 forbiddingt he clergy to administer sacraments.  John's refusal t
2 CONC o accept the newarch bishop led to his excommunication in 1209.  He regained papal favorby sur rendering his kingdom to Pope Innocent III but received it back asa pap al fief.
2 CONT The Magna Carta, reaffirming human rights, signed by John at Runnyme dein mid-June, 1215 limited the power of the English monarchy.  Feudal barons supported by Scotland's new king Alexander II met wit
2 CONC h John betweenS taines and Windsor, exacted major concessions reaffirming traditionalfeud al privileges contained in the accession charter signed by Henry I acentu ry before and compelled John to seth
2 CONC is seal to the Magna Carta.John imme diately appealed to Pope Innocent III, who issued a bullannulling the cha rter.  John imported French mercenaries to fight thebarons, but the Mag na Carta remained
2 CONC  the basis of English feudal justice.
2 CONT John came down with dysentery in October, 1216 after crushing resistan cein the north. He crossed the Wash and reached Newark Castle but died there October 19, 1216 at age 48. The king was succeeded b
2 CONC y his 9-year-olds on, John, who reigned until 1272 as Henry III; the earl of PembrokeWilli am Marshal served as regent, and the moderate party took control,ending t he need for opposition to royal aut
2 CONC hority.
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN I "Lackland" PLANTAGENET (King of England)
2 CONT Born: 24 Dec 1166, Beaumont Palace, Oxford, England
2 CONT Acceded: 27 May 1199, Westminster Abbey, London, England
2 CONT Died: 18/9 Oct 1216, Newark Castle, Newark, Nottinghamshire
2 CONT Buried: Worcester Cathedral
2 CONT Notes: Signed the Magna Carta at Runnymede, 1215. Reigned 1199-1216. His reign saw renewal of war with Phillip II Augustus of France to whom he has lost several continental possesions including Norman
2 CONC dy by 1205. He came into conflict with his Barons and was forced to Sign the Magna Carta. His later repudiation of the charter led to the first barons war 1215-17 during which John died. Burke says he
2 CONC  was born in 1160. King of Ireland 1177, Count of Mortain 1189, Earl of Gloucester. It is known that Agatha Ferrers was a mistress of John, but it is only supposition that she is the mother of Joan.
2 CONT Father: HENRY II PLANTAGENET (King of England)
2 CONT Mother: Eleanor of Aquitaine
2 CONT Married 1: Isabella FITZRICHARD (C. Gloucester) 29 Aug 1189, Marlborough Castle, Wiltshire Divorce 1199
2 CONT Married 2: Isabella of Angoulême (b. 1189 - d. 31 May 1246) (dau. of Aymer Taillefer, Count of Angoulême, and Alice De Courtenay) 24 Jun/Aug 1200, Bordeaux
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. HENRY III PLANTAGENET (King of England)
2 CONT 2. Richard PLANTAGENET (1º E. Cornwall)
2 CONT 3. Joan PLANTAGENET (Queen of Scotland)
2 CONT 4. Isabella PLANTAGENET (Empress of Germany)
2 CONT 5. Eleanor PLANTAGENET (C. Pembroke / C. Leicester)
2 CONT Associated with: Agatha De FERRERS
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Joan PLANTAGENETAssociated with: Clemence DAUNTSEY (wife of Henry Pinel)
2 CONT Associated with: Suzanne PLANTAGENET
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 7. Richard FITZJOHN (B. Chilham)
2 CONT Associated with: Hawise De TRACY
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 8. Oliver PLANTAGENET
2 CONT 9. Osbert GIFFORD (d. AFT 1216)
2 CONT 10. Geoffrey FITZROY
2 CONT 11. John FITZROY of Courcy (Knight or Clerk of Lincoln) (d. 1242)
2 CONT 12. Eudo FITZROY (d. ABT 1242)
2 CONT 13. Ivo FITZROY
2 CONT 14. Henry FITZROY
2 CONT 15. Richard FITZROY (Constable Wallingford Castle)
2 CONT 16. Matilda PLANTAGENET (Abbess of Barking)
2 CONT 17. Blanche (Isabella) PLANTAGENET
2 CONT
