3 CONT Why is there so many duplicates? Many are not even identified.
2 NOTE In September 1216 John began a fresh, vigorous attack. He marched from the Cotswolds, feigned an offensive to relieve the besieged Windsor Castle, and attacked eastwards around London to Cambridge to 
3 CONC separate the rebel-held areas of Lincolnshire and East Anglia. From there he travelled north to relieve the rebel siege at Lincoln and back east to King's Lynn, probably to order further supplies from
3 CONC  the continent. In King's Lynn, John contracted dysentery, which would ultimately prove fatal.
3 CONT
3 CONT Sidebar: If you ever in the England make it a point to go the Cotswolds. It is like driving in England 700 years ago. You can not build a house unless the outside looks and matches that period of time
3 CONC . 
